In .NET 10 (MAUI), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated/removed because Android itself deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE`. The recommended approach is now **edge-to-edge rendering with `WindowInsets` handling**.

## Solution

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`, enable edge-to-edge and use `WindowInsetsCompat` to add padding when the keyboard (IME) appears:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

        var rootView = Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!;

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or system bar bottom padding
            int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);

            v.SetPadding(
                systemBarInsets.Left,
                systemBarInsets.Top,
                systemBarInsets.Right,
                bottomPadding);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

## Key points

- **`SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(false)`** opts into edge-to-edge, letting your app draw behind system bars and the keyboard area.
- **`WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()`** gives you the keyboard height; you apply it as bottom padding so your input bar shifts up.
- This replaces the old `SoftInput = SoftInput.AdjustResize` / `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` pattern that Android deprecated in API 30+.

If you also want a smooth animation when the keyboard slides in, look into `WindowInsetsAnimationCompat.Callback` on the same root view.
